> I'm afraid not.

But I do. Make a per-user drop folder (for the affected users) and use a 
command-line tool to move mail from the per-user folders to the shared 
one. "mailutil move", I think. I think mailutil needs to be run as a 
separate user with the right to read and delete mail in he per-user 
spam folders.

This is an evil workaround, and like most evil workarounds, compliant 
with RFC 1925. In this case: You can ALWAYS add another level of 
indirection.

